WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is one of
my favorite shows on TV.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.869 line:92%
I've told you that before.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.904
It is -- it's very -- there are
moments that are really sad,

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:07.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's moments that are
incredibly intense.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:07.741 line:92%
But it's also very funny.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.943 size:81% position:41%
And there's moments of
great lightness to it.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.946
None of that lightness
came across in that clip.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:13.813 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. That is an incredibly
bleak clip, right?

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean, that just --

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can we do something fun?
-Sure.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:25.225
-Could we -- could we just watch
that clip -- and he's right.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:29.029
The rest of the season, it rocks
and it rolls and it's funny

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there is violence
and Gus is back and ugh.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.466 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Jonathan Banks, Mike.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.201 line:92%
But let's just watch it again.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:38.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you and I, let's just do
a DVD commentary

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:42.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
as though it were
a German experimental film.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, great.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.546 line:92%
-One more time and here we go.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ German accent ] So tell us
about this scene here.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:53.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ German accent ]
Well, the man is every man.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:53.586 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:57.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is lost in a lobby
in the middle of nowhere.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.259 size:75% position:38% line:92%
His life is plastic.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:02.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
All he owns is
in a little plastic bag.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:03.329 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.498 line:92%
-And what does she represent?

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.334 line:92%
-She represents humanity.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.402 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
All are numbers.
We are all numbers.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:12.472 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is lost. You see his body
is in the computer.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:16.176 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:20.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
His mind, he is alone,
and he will never get out.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:21.347 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.882
-[ Normal voice ] There you go.
That seems far more effective.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:27.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
Far more effective.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Normal voice ]
Would you watch that show?

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:30.990 line:92%
-I would watch that show.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.691 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I would watch any show

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:34.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was just two Germans
talking about things.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.530
So this is -- you know, this is
a prequel to "Breaking Bad."

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:37.964 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:42.735
-Saul, who we knew is still
Jimmy McGill in this show.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.572
-And did you create a back story
for this character?

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:49.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's so weird because I did
create a back -- just --

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.443 line:92%
When we went in to do the show,

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had to imagine who he was,
where did he grow up.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the things --
it's so funny

00:01:56.416 --> 00:02:00.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he went to the
University of American Samoa.

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:01.421 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We know that.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:05.892
And I just made up in my head
that he was in a fraternity.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:06.426 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:09.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I made up these friends
and I gave them names.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were --
this is for real --

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
Michael Avenatti
and Michael Cohen.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:15.768 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:16.903 line:92%
And that was their names.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just picked them
out of nowhere.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:21.608 size:84% position:42%
I didn't know anyone --
and then I -- Get this.

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:24.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
His professor,
his favorite professor,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.612 line:92%
was a guy named Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:28.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's perfect.
That all makes sense now.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:31.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it --
I predicted the future.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:34.220
-Well, it -- you really did,
because I feel like before --

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
and again,
there have been some examples,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
but a lot of times
lawyers on television

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.059 size:88% position:44% line:92%
have a lot of integrity.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And we watch them.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
They fight for
what's right and justice.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:44.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Jimmy McGill/Saul,
none of that.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:49.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not a man of -- a man who is
willing to cut corners,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:49.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should say.
-Yes.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now the lawyers on TV
we're seeing are real lawyers.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.942
-They're worse than Saul.
-They're worse than Saul.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:59.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Saul is like a really
good guy, comparatively,

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the real world.
-Yes.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:01.514 line:92%
And that's nice to watch.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.617 size:84% position:42%
Do you think Saul would
represent Donald Trump

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
if he was asked?

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do think he would.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:09.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do think.
He would love the limelight.

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:09.889 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And he would --

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think they'd have
a bit of a mind meld

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:13.393 line:92%
with how to handle things.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:16.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do -- he might have an issue
with getting paid.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:17.430 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.531 line:92%
-The whole "I don't pay people,

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:21.601 size:78% position:39%
it should be an honor
to just work for me."

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.235 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I think he'd --

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.604 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah, Saul famously
likes to get paid.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.539 line:92%
-You're gonna pay me somehow.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.340 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were in --
this is very exciting --

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.411 line:92%
you were in "The Incredibles."

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:31.844 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your voice was in
the new "Incredibles" movie.

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:34.614 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Winston Deavor.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:39.352 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:43.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, they asked --
I was such -- so honored

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.291 line:92%
to be asked to be in this movie.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I talked to Brad Bird,
the director,

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:50.997
and the first thing I said was,
"Thank you.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:52.699 line:92%
I'll -- Of course I'll do it.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:56.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
But could you make him
not look like me?"

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:57.070 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Could you make him
look like Seth Meyers?"

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.874 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.676 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.812 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Actually --

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:11.918 size:84% position:42%
I mean, really. Really.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.087 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Heartbreaking.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:14.654 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly you.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:18.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, to make it look like
that and not cast me,

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.626 size:88% position:44% line:92%
they must hate my voice.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.293 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.728 line:92%
Just hate my voice so much.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:24.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-His face is perfect for
animation.

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.399 size:81% position:41% line:92%
The nose and the hair.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:27.100 line:92%
But the voice won't work.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The vo-- it just doesn't --
it doesn't work at all.

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:32.672 line:92%
-It won't stick to the tape.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.507 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We tried it.

